source_caption:
In this early scene from Goodfellas (1990), a teenage Henry Hill goes to court for the first time. When the judge asks him to testify against the local mob, he says nothing. Outside the courthouse, mobster Jimmy Conway (Robert De Niro) congratulates Henry, telling him he learned the “two greatest things in life;” “never rat on your friends, and always keep your mouth shut.” 

